ools.exec_command({cmd:\"cat > /home/ubuntu/tiered-breakdown-evidence/audit/AUDIT.md <<'EOF'\\n# Breakdown measurement audit\\n\\nThe new diagnostics are not non-invasive. The earlier successful end-to-end runs\\nproved marker presence, artifact production and algebraic partition consistency;\\nthey did not prove negligible timing perturbation.\\n\\n## Direct comparison through the real offline driver\\n\\nSame GH200, Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct, CD3 fused weights + CD3 KV, fixed random-input\\nworkload (batch 16, 1020 input tokens, 33 generated tokens, prefill chunk 8192),\\ndedicated KV blocks 16, planner blocks 4096, first 4 decode intervals excluded.\\nBoth arms used `--time-breakdown`; this compares the new addition against the old\\ninstrumented breakdown, not against uninstrumented production.\\n\\nBefore: detached checkout of f4ab632457015f416d7d09ebde83f284d6062582.\\nAfter: live container checkout of the same base plus the delivered breakdown\\nchanges. Native codec sources and all workload options were the same. Before ran\\nfirst, after second, in fresh processes, one run each. This is a finite diagnostic\\ncomparison, not a statistical equivalence claim or a bound over all workloads.\\n\\n| Metric | Before | After |\\n|---|---:|---:|\\n| TPOT mean, ms | 132.98 | 158.20 |\\n| Model-forward mean, ms | 93.5476 | 93.753154 |\\n| Recorded exposed-load mean, ms | 13.6696 | 13.632952 |\\n| Logged weight-ready wait sum, ms | 4.92 | 2.94 |\\n\\nThe TPOT increase is 18.97%; the model-forward difference is +0.22%.\\nThe model comparison uses the new `model_fwd_ms`, excluding the new logits scope.\\nBoth runs had the same phase/token-count sequence and identical dense-equivalent\\nKV byte totals; H2D payload means differed by about 0.0003%. Wait distributions\\nare not proven unchanged, and this pair does not isolate the cause of their change.\\nMachine-readable engine-step results are in `comparison.json`; raw outputs and\\nlogs are under `before/` and `after/`.\\n\\nA supporting replay of 20 previously recorded decode-forward interval sets through\\nthe exact CPU analysis + CSV writer took median 21.036 ms, mean 22.480 ms. This\\nmeasures only postprocessing on stored data, not CUDA execution, and is not a\\nsubstitute for the real comparison above. It supports a substantial CPU cost.\\n\\n## What is and is not measured\\n\\n- CPU analysis and CSV flushing happen after end-event synchronization. They do\\n  not enter the completed forward's GPU timestamp difference, but delay token\\n  delivery and subsequent steps. They can change serving batch formation and\\n  the time available to asynchronous KV workers.\\n- There are approximately 400 prefetch event records per 80-layer forward, plus\\n  auxiliary markers. They execute on the GPU timeline and are not zero-cost.\\n- Collection moved from model completion to logits completion and now performs\\n  device-wide synchronization. This changes the observer's synchronization scope.\\n- The interval sweep correctly partitions recorded event windows. This does not\\n  prove pure DMA/SM busy time, total GPU idle time or an unperturbed schedule.\\n- Prefetch's compute-stream marker is not CPU submission time. In the previous\\n  real serving run, 43,802 of 45,520 defined marker-to-H2D gaps were negative.\\n  Treating these as copy-engine queue delays would be incorrect. CPU and GPU\\n  issue columns have distinct origins, with no calibrated correlation.\\n- Ready/lateness use the latest observed producer end before wait end, not the\\n  actual sync barrier timestamp or a proof that all tensor prerequisites ended.\\n- Auxiliary marker presence and exact state sums are bookkeeping checks, not\\n  independent verification of zero interference or kernel-only elapsed time.\\n\\nCUDA's own reference explicitly documents asynchronous event recording, possible\\nintervening stream work and approximately 0.5 microsecond timing resolution:\\nhttps://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/cuda-runtime-api/cuda_runtime_api/group__CUDART__EVENT.html\\n\\nFurther correction should move bulk CPU analysis/output out of the inference\\ncritical path, preserve a clearly named model-only comparison window, and either\\nprovide a valid host/GPU correlation for enqueue latency or retain explicitly\\nnamed scheduling-marker proxies. No production source was changed during this\\naudit. Both comparison processes exited successfully; the temporary baseline\\nworktree was removed after preserving its results.\\nEOF\",\"max_output_tokens\":1000}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0a9db-4e67-7e23-b253-8fc31b61e2a7","create_time":1789556708.200712}}}
